i couldn't find it either, so i jerry-rigged a fake conditional breakpoint with a framework checkout. the call stack responsible for the hide is:

```
SliderSelectionBlueprint.LoadComplete();
SelectionBlueprint<HitObject>.LoadComplete();
SelectionBlueprint<HitObject>.updateState();
SliderSelectionBlueprint.OnDeselected();
SelectionBlueprint<HitObject>.OnDeselected();
```

however this call stack being this generic makes me wonder whether other blueprints that delegate to their drawable contents in `ReceivePositionalInputAt()` are affected as well. it sure as hell feels like they should be.

i think this might warrant more looking-into. if this is indeed slider-specific then i'd probably also mention what hides the internal child to spare future travelers this same ordeal.
